2:T7e8,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the average kitchen fitting cost per unit in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, standard cabinet installation labour may typically be around £150–£300 per unit. Tall, integrated or complex units may be around £250–£500 or more. Every project differs, and these figures commonly exclude kitchen furniture and additional trades; request a free, no-obligation quote from BMB Renovation for accurate pricing in its service areas."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is kitchen fitting charged per unit or by the day?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Both approaches may be used. Per-unit pricing can suit a straightforward installation, while a daily rate or fixed project price may be more suitable where there is removal, plumbing, tiling, electrical work or extensive preparation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the cost per kitchen unit include appliances?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often it does not. Appliance supply may be separate, and installation may also be separate if connections, housing alterations, ventilation or electrical work are required. Check each appliance and connection on the written quote."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What makes kitchen fitting more expensive?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Complex layouts, uneven walls or floors, islands, tall units, bespoke finishes, stone worktops, appliance changes, plumbing, electrics, tiling, flooring and plastering can all increase the total cost."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I get an accurate kitchen fitting price?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Provide a measured plan, cabinet schedule, appliance list and worktop details, then ask for a written quote that separates fitting, removal, materials and additional trades. A site visit can help check access and the condition of the room. BMB Renovation offers free, no-obligation quotes."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-fitting-cost-per-unit-uk","d"]
